{"chunk_id": "db3af1e07709", "text": "This section recounts the origin of two crucial figures of the Mahabharata: Dhrishtadyumna and Draupadi. King Drupada, humiliated by the warrior\u2011teacher Drona, seeks a son destined to kill him. With the help of the Brahmins Yaja and Upayaja, he performs a powerful fire sacrifice. From the sacrificial flames emerges a fully armed son, Dhrishtadyumna, prophesied to destroy Drona and restore Panchala\u2019s honor. Immediately afterward a daughter, the dark\u2011complexioned and extraordinarily beautiful Panchali (Draupadi), is born, foretold to bring about the downfall of many Kshatriyas and great danger to the Kauravas. Ironically, Drona himself later trains the boy destined to kill him, accepting fate. Hearing this tale unsettles the Pandavas, and Kunti suggests they journey to Panchala.\nDrupada\u2019s sacrifice produces Dhrishtadyumna destined to kill Drona and the princess Draupadi, after which Kunti urges the Pandavas to journey to Panchala.\nThemes: destiny and prophecy, sacrificial birth, revenge against Drona, divine intervention, future downfall of Kshatriyas", "vector": [-0.002067938446998596, -0.016971470788121223, -0.007950779981911182, 0.00042921840213239193, -0.016904601827263832, 0.03378245607018471, -0.018455972895026207, 0.0028770589269697666, -0.007516128476709127, -0.01341401506215334, 0.013072981499135494, 0.029663296416401863, 0.0042863329872488976, 0.023096714168787003, 0.009381786920130253, 0.025584258139133453, 0.04057639464735985, -0.017559923231601715, 0.02734961360692978, -0.03889128193259239, 0.003075995482504368, -0.02265537530183792, 0.01451067440211773, 0.03164263442158699, -0.02242802083492279, 0.039452988654375076, 0.019606128334999084, -0.0198736060410738, 0.006880868226289749, -0.008138014003634453, -0.017573297023773193, 0.00043799501145258546, 0.004386637359857559, -0.006018252111971378, -0.01578119397163391, 0.003905177116394043, -0.0017837430350482464, -0.013233467936515808, 0.0068440902